        "id": "s1_androecium",
        "kind": "text",
        "label": "Androecium",
        "marks": 1,
        "lines": [
          "The essential floral parts are the two whorls",
          "that take part in reproduction: the androecium",
          "and the gynoecium.",
          "Androecium:",
          "Six stamens in two whorls of three (3+3).",
          "They are free and epiphyllous, attached to the",
          "perianth.",
          "Anthers are dithecous, basifixed and introrse,",
          "and open by longitudinal dehiscence."
        ],
        "why": "Only the androecium and gynoecium are essential; naming that first shows the examiner you have read the word \"essential\".",
        "common_mistakes": [
          "Describing the perianth. The perianth is not an essential part.",
          "Writing epipetalous instead of epiphyllous. Liliaceae has tepals, not petals."
        ],
        "memory_tip": "Everything in Liliaceae comes in threes: 3+3 tepals, 3+3 stamens, 3 carpels.",
        "margin_note": "Head the block \"Androecium\" and give four short technical terms.",
        "mark_note": "Androecium"
      },
      {
        "id": "s2_gynoecium",
        "kind": "text",
        "label": "Gynoecium",
        "marks": 1,
        "lines": [
          "Gynoecium:",
          "Tricarpellary and syncarpous, with a trilocular",
          "superior ovary.",
          "Placentation is axile; each locule holds many",
          "ovules.",
          "The style is terminal and the stigma is trifid and",
          "capitate."
        ],
        "why": "Three fused carpels give three chambers, and three chambers with a central column is exactly what axile placentation means.",
        "common_mistakes": [
          "Writing parietal placentation. A trilocular fused ovary has axile placentation.",
          "Writing inferior ovary. In Liliaceae the ovary is superior."
        ],
        "memory_tip": "Three carpels joined gives three locules, and the join in the middle is the axis the ovules sit on.",
        "margin_note": "Head the block \"Gynoecium\". Five terms, one line each.",
        "mark_note": "Gynoecium"
      },
