        "why": "The L.S. shows where the stamens are attached and that the ovary sits above the other whorls; the T.S. shows the three locules and the central placenta that the words describe.",
        "common_mistakes": [
          "Drawing two locules in the T.S. Liliaceae is trilocular.",
          "Putting the ovules on the ovary wall. In axile placentation they sit on the central axis."
        ],
        "memory_tip": "Draw the circle, cut it into three with three lines from the centre, and put the ovules where the three lines meet.",
        "margin_note": "The T.S. of the ovary alone can carry this mark. Label ovary wall, locule, ovule and placenta."
